{"title":"2003 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Calculus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Calculus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/9/bf930f4352386aa16fcd2f632835d5b2d7a5a5d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq b &gt; 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> what is the largest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/2/e82e6bb11cc78c2205b4010f66b0380278dce195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{a}(a/b) + \\log_{b}(b/a)?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"173\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/7267bfd95303541b2fd3f538aad0d9996284ff2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ -2      \\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\ 0     \\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\ 2      \\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\ 3      \\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\ 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"364\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using logarithmic rules, we see that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/8/ac81a63197833883d0f23b2c94e96af4303e9c3e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_{a}a-\\log_{a}b+\\log_{b}b-\\log_{b}a = 2-(\\log_{a}b+\\log_{b}a)\\]\" width=\"412\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/2/4f29ea1ef11f63ecbc83a12100f5efbfb171530e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=2-\\left(\\log_{a}b+\\frac {1}{\\log_{a}b}\\right)\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are both greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, using <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-GM\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-GM\">AM-GM</a> gives that the term in parentheses must be at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the largest possible values is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/f/9efb2ae2c036e29658700b4a6ed9031c7c921b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2-2=0 \\Rightarrow \\boxed{\\textbf{B}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>Note that the maximum occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5abd2c942ae299fd26e18d0ca5d390a7ca4a8c34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Calculus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Calculus)\">Solution 2 (Calculus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Calculus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the logarithmic rules, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/2/e02bac793e9817a6da6331c7ff068a1686f6ebe0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2-(\\log_a{b}+\\frac{1}{\\log_a{b}})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"158\" height=\"43\" />.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/3/1b30a3f33228504cc1509bc104ceb78f0eaf9d89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\log_a{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"17\" />. Thus, the expression becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55ba45f3ab29737807a5e05d8392145749718295.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2-(x+\\frac{1}{x})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" />. We want to find the maximum of the function. To do so, we will find its derivative and let it equal to 0. We get: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/d/3cd5eaa2ff0bc80b7bf6ab7de843d9b2bc919b20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{dx}\\big(2-(x+\\frac{1}{x})\\big)=\\frac{d}{dx}\\big(2-x-\\frac{1}{x})=-1+x^{-2}=0 \\implies \\frac{1}{x^2}=1, x^2=1, x=\\pm1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"642\" height=\"39\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/d/d6d47810abd97c27886e605b92f960af1e97a9b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\geq b&gt;1, x=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" /> is not a solution. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Substituting it into the original expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55ba45f3ab29737807a5e05d8392145749718295.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2-(x+\\frac{1}{x})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/8/8c8b7fc390e116ba8c77b57c57f6490c30186403.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2-(1+\\frac{1}{1})=2-2=\\boxed{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"201\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The Link: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=InF2phZZi2A&amp;t=1s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=InF2phZZi2A&amp;t=1s</a>\n</p><p>-MistyMathMusic\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><sp